er failed to raise equity.** It withdrew its planned C$2.4B equity offering because investor demand fell short. It is also the largest single buyer of grid equipment in Caldria and plans 2027 capex up 18%. It says it will cut 2027 transformer orders by about 40% and defer two substation programmes until financing improves. So the equity shortfall is already reducing spending.\n- **The wider equity market is weak.** In Q3 2026, two utility share offerings were cut back in size.\n- **Debt is open, at a higher price.** Utility bond spreads widened 30bp in Q3 to 165bp. Norvane Utilities (2027 capex up 12%) priced a C$1.1B bond comfortably.\n\n**Conclusion:** Equity can fill small gaps, and offerings that are smaller or priced at a discount may still get done. It can't carry large raises like Pellham's C$2.4B. Utilities should lean on debt, which means higher financing costs. Pellham-type programmes will likely be deferred or cut until financing improves.\n\n**Caveat:** The evidence mainly describes Pellham and Norvane. I have no data on other Caldrian utilities.","ttft_ms":3890,"type":"result","duration_ms":21927,"uuid":"2435544a-cc08-4a22-acee-b3ffba42b6bb","ttft_stream_ms":2630,"time_to_request_ms":74,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":5,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":4,"input_attachments":14,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":4,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":9,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":3,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":3,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":24,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":72,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":203,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":131,"process_rss_mib_result":203,"process_anon_mib_result":123,"process_peak_rss_mib":222,"pro